# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 5 of the Tutorial (Part 1)

[Bo2's Drill Exercise 3.2]

e,1,0,.1
r12,1,2,1'k
r2o,2,o,10'k
r30,3,0,1'k
r3o,3,o,20'k
o,3,2,o

analysis: dc
note: In this problem, we use an ideal op amp (the o element) for the first time. Find vo and the power absorbed by the op amp. The op amp's power is negative, so it delivers 0.63 mW to the circuit rather than absorbing it.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/bo2de0302.jpg [490px]
rounding: 2
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 3.11 (Thevenin)]

e,1,0,vs
r1,2,0,r1
r2,2,3,r2
o,1,2,3

analysis: dc
note: Find the Thévenin equivalent of the op-amp circuit. The tricky one. An ideal op amp holds its output voltage whatever current is drawn, so the short-circuit round has no solution -- and until 0.5.13 the whole answer was lost with it. Symbulator now measures the short instead of assuming it, and reports what the chapter asserts but never shows: the Norton current is unbounded and the Thevenin resistance is 0.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-3-11-thevenin-1.jpg [579px]
tool: th
n1: 3
n2: 0
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


