[TR5's Exercise 4-11 (Inverting)]

e,1,0,vs
r1,1,2,10'k
r2,2,o,33'k
o,0,2,o

analysis: dc
note: Find vo when vs is 2 V, -4 V and 6 V. The Evaluate line answers vs = 2: -6.6 V. For the other two, put vs = -4 then vs = 6 in Evaluate's Conditions box: 13.2 and -19.8. The op amp is limited to +/-15 V, so the real answer for vs = 6 is -15.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/tr5s-exercise-4-11-inverting-7.jpg [514px]
rounding: 3
si: no
units: yes
evaluate: vo
evaluate_conditions: vs = 2
plottool: sweep
plotkey: v_o
plotx: vs
plotmin: 0
plotmax: 10
plotpoints: 300


