[TR5's Example 4-13 (Non-Inverting, in one)]

e,1,0,vs
r1,1,2,r1
r2,2,0,r2
o,2,3,o
r3,o,3,r3
r4,3,0,r4

analysis: dc
note: Find Vo/Vs in a single simulation: r2*(r3+r4)/((r1+r2)*r4).
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/tr5s-example-4-13-non-inverting-amplifier-18.jpg [520px]
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes
evaluate: vo/vs


[TR5's Example 4-13 (the left half)]

e,1,0,vs
r1,1,2,r1
r2,2,0,r2

analysis: dc
note: The same problem solved in stages: the left half's voltage divider gives v2/vs = r2/(r1+r2).
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/tr5s-example-4-13-non-inverting-amplifier-18.jpg [520px]
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes
evaluate: v2/vs


[TR5's Example 4-13 (the right half)]

e,2,0,1
o,2,3,o
r3,o,3,r3
r4,3,0,r4

analysis: dc
note: The right half gives vo/v2 = (r3+r4)/r4. The product of this and the previous entry is the whole circuit's gain.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/tr5s-example-4-13-non-inverting-amplifier-18.jpg [520px]
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes
evaluate: vo/v2


