[TR5's Figure 4-32 (Voltage Follower, the source alone)]

e,1,0,1.5
rs,1,2,2'k

analysis: dc
note: The bare source of circuit (b): find its maximum power and the power a 1 kohm load would draw. The load question comes ticked, and the Evaluate line reads prl at load = 1000, the chapter's prL|L=1000.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/tr5s-figure-4-32-voltage-follower-21.jpg
tool: th
n1: 2
n2: 0
with_load: yes
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
evaluate: prl
evaluate_conditions: load = 1000


[TR5's Figure 4-32 (Voltage Follower, buffered)]

e,1,0,1.5
rs,1,2,2'k
o,2,o,o
rl,o,0,1'k

analysis: dc
note: Circuit (a): the same source buffered by a voltage follower. Find prl, the power in the 1 kohm load: 2.25 mW. The load draws more than the bare source could deliver, because the ideal op amp in the schematic stands in for a real one with its own supply.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/tr5s-figure-4-32-voltage-follower-21.jpg
rounding: 3
si: no
units: yes


